# flickos-menu: the start menu, the apps button's default (flickos-layouts
# >= 1.23); nothing of it runs while a user has it off. A Depends so
# installed systems get it: FlickOS doesn't install new Recommends.
         flickos-menu (>= 1.0),
# flickos-welcome: the window a new account sees once at its first login. A
# Depends so installed systems get it; nothing of it runs afterwards.
         flickos-welcome,
# flickos-phone: pages, files and text from and to a phone. Off by default,
# and nothing of it runs while off. A Depends so installed systems get it
# (docs/design/flickos-phone.md, ADR-002).
         flickos-phone,
# flickos-screenshot: screenshots (the Print keys, Super+Shift+S, the menus).
# Nothing of it runs until a key is pressed (docs/design/flickos-screenshot.md,
# ADR-002). A Depends so installed systems get it; flickos-settings (>= 1.31)'s
# keys run it.
         flickos-screenshot,
# flickos-countme: the anonymous weekly count (PRIVACY.md). A Depends so
# installed systems get it: new installs are asked in the installer, systems
# installed before it are counted until they turn it off in Settings ->
# Privacy (opt-out).
         flickos-countme,
# brightness-udev: brightnessctl's udev rule, which lets the video group
# (every FlickOS account and the live user) set the backlight. Without it the
# brightness keys and Quick Settings' slider do nothing: Debian's brightnessctl
# doesn't go through logind. A Depends so installed systems get it.
         brightness-udev,
# flickos-software: Software, the window that installs and removes Debian's
# and Flathub's apps; it replaces gnome-packagekit's gpk-application (design
# ADR-010). A Depends so installed systems get it; nothing of it runs while
# the window is closed, except a daily timer that updates Flatpak apps.
         flickos-software,
# flickos-recovery: a restore point before every software change, on the btrfs
# layout new installs get; on ext4 nothing of it runs (the apt hook leaves at
# once). A Depends so installed systems get it (docs/design/flickos-recovery.md,
# ADR-006).
         flickos-recovery,
# zstd: initramfs-tools' COMPRESS=zstd needs the zstd program; without it
# update-initramfs falls back to gzip, which makes a larger initramfs that
# GRUB reads and the kernel unpacks more slowly at every start
# (docs/design/flickos-recovery.md, phase 1a). A Depends so installed systems
# get it; their next initramfs rebuild uses it.
         zstd,
         ${misc:Depends}
# Recommends: removable apps and tools. Users can uninstall any of these
# without apt also removing flickos-desktop.
